From: =?utf-8?b?T3R0byBLZWvDpGzDpGluZW4=?= <otto@debian.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Mar 2026 13:52:57 +0000
Subject: Remove DEPENDS in MERGE_STATIC_LIBS macro to fix CMake CMP0175
 warning

The DEPENDS keyword is not valid for add_custom_command() with a TARGET
signature. CMake 3.27+ warns about this via policy CMP0175.

The generated MRI script is created in the same directory as the build
output and is written by FILE(GENERATE) immediately before the custom
command runs, so an explicit dependency is unnecessary.

Fixes warning:

    CMake Warning (dev) at cmake/libutils.cmake:229 (ADD_CUSTOM_COMMAND):
      The following keywords are not supported when using
      add_custom_command(TARGET): DEPENDS.

      Policy CMP0175 is not set: add_custom_command() rejects invalid arguments.
      Run "cmake --help-policy CMP0175" for policy details.  Use the cmake_policy
      command to set the policy and suppress this warning.
    Call Stack (most recent call first):
      cmake/libutils.cmake:267 (MERGE_STATIC_LIBS)
      libmysqld/CMakeLists.txt:207 (MERGE_LIBRARIES)
---
 cmake/libutils.cmake | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/libutils.cmake b/cmake/libutils.cmake
index 8fd8f32..a7a43d8 100644
--- a/cmake/libutils.cmake
+++ b/cmake/libutils.cmake
@@ -227,7 +227,6 @@ MACRO(MERGE_STATIC_LIBS TARGET OUTPUT_NAME LIBS_TO_MERGE)
       FILE(GENERATE OUTPUT ${MRI_SCRIPT} INPUT ${MRI_SCRIPT_TPL})
 
       ADD_CUSTOM_COMMAND(TARGET ${TARGET} POST_BUILD
-        DEPENDS ${MRI_SCRIPT}
         COMMAND ${CMAKE_COMMAND}
         ARGS
           -DTARGET_SCRIPT="${MRI_SCRIPT}"
